      "body": "## Finding Summary\n\nWhen the CL pool’s rewards are updated during periods with zero staked liquidity, the contract consumes time and reduces reserves into a `rollover` bucket, but later `syncReward()` deletes `rollover`. The consequence is rewards streamed in such empty windows are lost.\n\n\nIn `_updateRewardsGrowthGlobal()` , when `timeDelta != 0` and `rewardReserve > 0`, it calculates rewards: `reward = rewardRate * timeDelta` and deducts them from the `rewardReserve`\n\nWhen stakedLiquidity == 0, it adds the reward to rollover.\n```solidity\nif (stakedLiquidity > 0) {\n                    rewardGrowthGlobalX128 += FullMath.mulDiv(reward, FixedPoint128.Q128, stakedLiquidity);\n                } else {\n                    rollover += reward;\n                }\n```\nIt always updates `lastUpdated = timestamp` regardless of whether there's `stakedLiquidity`\n\n\nIn `syncReward()`, rollover is deleted after setting new reward parameters.\n\nSo the rewards streamed during periods with zero staked liquidity get tracked in rollover, but `syncReward()` deletes this rollover, causing those rewards to be lost forever.\n\n\n\n## Impact\n\nLoss of matured yield: Users cannot claim rewards corresponding to empty windows.\n\nThis also violates two invariants:\n[G-2] Balance Conservation: \"On-chain balances must always be greater than or equal to the sum of all accrued/claimable balances (rewards, bribes, fees)\"\n[R-2] Monotone Accrual: rewards should accrue monotonically - as here they disappear\n\n## Mitigation\n\nIf `stakedLiquidity == 0`, do not advance `lastUpdated` and do not decrement `rewardReserve`.",
      "proofOfConcept": "## PoC\n\nPaste this in ve33/C4PoC.t.sol. It shows approximately 42 tokens are lost after the rewards sync.\n\n```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity 0.8.13;\n\nimport \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\n\nimport {C4PoCTestbed} from \"./C4PoCTestbed.t.sol\";\nimport {IERC20} from \"@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC20/IERC20.sol\";\n/**\n * @title C4PoC\n * @notice A complete deployment of the CL contract suite\n * @dev All available variables are showcased in the commented\n *      storage slots of the contract.\n */\n\ncontract C4PoC is C4PoCTestbed {\n    \n    address public testPool;\n    address public testGauge;\n    address public testToken0;\n    address public testToken1;\n    \n    address public alice = makeAddr(\"alice\");\n    address public keeper = makeAddr(\"keeper\");\n    \n    function setUp() public override {\n        super.setUp();\n        \n        testToken0 = address(0x1000000000000000000000000000000000000001); // Mock token\n        testToken1 = address(0x2000000000000000000000000000000000000002); // Mock token\n        \n        // @audit - Deploy mock ERC20s\n        vm.etch(testToken0, type(MockERC20).runtimeCode);\n        vm.etch(testToken1, type(MockERC20).runtimeCode);\n        \n        MockERC20(testToken0).initialize(\"Token0\", \"TK0\", 18);\n        MockERC20(testToken1).initialize(\"Token1\", \"TK1\", 18);\n        \n        // Create pool using the factory from testbed\n        testPool = ICLPoolFactory(clPoolFactory).createPool(\n            testToken0,\n            testToken1,\n            50,\n            encodePriceSqrt(1, 1)\n        );\n        \n        // Get gauge address from pool\n        testGauge = ICLPoolMinimal(testPool).gauge();\n        \n        console.log(\"=== Test Setup Complete ===\");\n        console.log(\"Test Pool:\", testPool);\n        console.log(\"Test Gauge:\", testGauge);\n    }\n    \n    function test_submissionValidity5_RolloverLossWhenNoStakedLiquidity() public {\n        console.log(\"\\n=== STARTING POC: Rollover Loss During Zero Staked Liquidity ===\\n\");\n        \n        // Step 1: Fund the gauge with rewards and notify the pool\n        uint256 rewardAmount = 100 ether;\n        deal(address(hybr), testGauge, rewardAmount);\n        \n        console.log(\"Step 1: Initial reward funding\");\n        console.log(\"  Reward amount:\", rewardAmount);\n        \n        // Calculate reward rate for 1 week\n        uint256 rewardRate = rewardAmount / 1 weeks;\n        uint256 periodFinish = block.timestamp + 1 weeks;\n        \n        // Gauge calls syncReward on the pool (simulating distribution)\n        vm.prank(testGauge);\n        ICLPoolMinimal(testPool).syncReward(rewardRate, rewardAmount, periodFinish);\n        \n        uint256 initialReserve = ICLPoolMinimal(testPool).rewardReserve();\n        uint256 initialRollover = ICLPoolMinimal(testPool).rollover();\n        uint128 initialStakedLiq = ICLPoolMinimal(testPool).stakedLiquidity();\n        \n        console.log(\"\\n  Initial state:\");\n        console.log(\"    Reward Reserve:\", initialReserve);\n        console.log(\"    Rollover:\", initialRollover);\n        console.log(\"    Staked Liquidity:\", initialStakedLiq);\n        \n        assertEq(initialReserve, rewardAmount, \"Initial reserve should equal reward amount\");\n        assertEq(initialRollover, 0, \"Initial rollover should be 0\");\n        assertEq(initialStakedLiq, 0, \"No staked liquidity yet\");\n        \n        // Step 2: Time passes with NO staked liquidity\n        // Rewards will be consumed and added to rollover\n        uint256 timeElapsed = 3 days;\n        vm.warp(block.timestamp + timeElapsed);\n        \n        console.log(\"\\nStep 2: Time passes with zero staked liquidity\");\n        console.log(\"  Time elapsed:\", timeElapsed, \"seconds (3 days)\");\n        \n        // @audit simulate Trigger update (this happens during swaps)\n        vm.prank(testGauge);\n        ICLPoolMinimal(testPool).updateRewardsGrowthGlobal();\n        \n        uint256 reserveAfterTime = ICLPoolMinimal(testPool).rewardReserve();\n        uint256 rolloverAfterTime = ICLPoolMinimal(testPool).rollover();\n        uint128 stakedLiqAfterTime = ICLPoolMinimal(testPool).stakedLiquidity();\n        \n        console.log(\"\\n  State after time passes:\");\n        console.log(\"    Reward Reserve:\", reserveAfterTime);\n        console.log(\"    Rollover:\", rolloverAfterTime);\n        console.log(\"    Staked Liquidity:\", stakedLiqAfterTime);\n        \n        // Calculate expected consumed rewards\n        uint256 expectedConsumed = rewardRate * timeElapsed;\n        console.log(\"\\n  Expected rewards consumed:\", expectedConsumed);\n        console.log(\"  Actual rewards in rollover:\", rolloverAfterTime);\n        \n        // Verify rewards moved to rollover (not distributed since stakedLiquidity == 0)\n        assertApproxEqAbs(\n            initialReserve - reserveAfterTime,\n            expectedConsumed,\n            1e15, // Small tolerance for rounding\n            \"Rewards should have been consumed from reserve\"\n        );\n        \n        assertApproxEqAbs(\n            rolloverAfterTime,\n            expectedConsumed,\n            1e15,\n            \"Consumed rewards should be in rollover\"\n        );\n        \n        assertEq(stakedLiqAfterTime, 0, \"Still no staked liquidity\");\n        \n        // Step 3: syncReward is called (e.g., next epoch, keeper, or governance)\n        console.log(\"\\nStep 3: syncReward called - DELETES ROLLOVER\");\n        \n        vm.prank(testGauge);\n        ICLPoolMinimal(testPool).syncReward(\n            rewardRate,\n            reserveAfterTime,\n            block.timestamp + 4 days\n        );\n        \n        uint256 finalReserve = ICLPoolMinimal(testPool).rewardReserve();\n        uint256 finalRollover = ICLPoolMinimal(testPool).rollover();\n        \n        console.log(\"\\n  State after syncReward:\");\n        console.log(\"    Reward Reserve:\", finalReserve);\n        console.log(\"    Rollover:\", finalRollover);\n        console.log(\"    ROLLOVER DELETED - REWARDS LOST:\", rolloverAfterTime);\n        \n        assertEq(finalRollover, 0, \"Rollover was deleted by syncReward\");\n        \n        // Step 4: Even when liquidity arrives, those rewards are gone forever\n        console.log(\"\\nStep 4: Liquidity arrives later (too late!)\");\n        \n        vm.warp(block.timestamp + 1 days);\n        \n        // Simulate someone staking liquidity now\n        // (In real code, this would go through gauge.deposit -> pool.stake)\n        vm.prank(testGauge);\n        ICLPoolMinimal(testPool).stake(\n            1 ether, // Add 1 ether of staked liquidity\n            -100, // tickLower\n            100,  // tickUpper\n            false // positionUpdate\n        );\n        \n        uint128 finalStakedLiq = ICLPoolMinimal(testPool).stakedLiquidity();\n        console.log(\"  Staked Liquidity now:\", finalStakedLiq);\n        \n        // Trigger reward update with liquidity present\n        vm.prank(testGauge);\n        ICLPoolMinimal(testPool).updateRewardsGrowthGlobal();\n        \n        uint256 rewardGrowth = ICLPoolMinimal(testPool).rewardGrowthGlobalX128();\n        \n        console.log(\"  Reward Growth Global:\", rewardGrowth);\n        console.log(\"  Remaining Reserve:\", ICLPoolMinimal(testPool).rewardReserve());\n        \n\n        uint256 totalLost = rolloverAfterTime;\n\n        console.log(\"Total rewards PERMANENTLY LOST:\", totalLost);\n        console.log(\"Percentage of initial funding lost:\", (totalLost * 100) / rewardAmount, \"%\");\n        console.log(\"\\nThis violates invariants:\");\n        console.log(\"  [G-2] Balance Conservation\");\n        console.log(\"  [R-2] Monotone Accrual\");\n        console.log(\"\\nRewards were:\");\n        console.log(\"  1. Funded by governance/minter\");\n        console.log(\"  2. Consumed from rewardReserve\");\n        console.log(\"  3. Placed in rollover (because stakedLiquidity == 0)\");\n        console.log(\"  4. DELETED by syncReward\");\n        console.log(\"  5. Never claimable by any user\");\n        console.log(\"========================================\\n\");\n        \n        // @audit Final assertions proving the bug\n        assertTrue(totalLost > 0, \"Rewards must have been lost\");\n        assertEq(finalRollover, 0, \"Rollover must have been deleted\");\n        assertGt(totalLost, rewardAmount / 10, \"Significant amount lost (>10% of funding)\");\n    }\n    \n    // Helper: Encode sqrt price from ratio\n    function encodePriceSqrt(uint256 reserve1, uint256 reserve0) internal pure returns (uint160) {\n        return uint160(sqrt((reserve1 * 2**192) / reserve0));\n    }\n    \n    // Helper: Square root calculation\n    function sqrt(uint256 x) internal pure returns (uint256 y) {\n        if (x == 0) return 0;\n        uint256 z = (x + 1) / 2;\n        y = x;\n        while (z < y) {\n            y = z;\n            z = (x / z + z) / 2;\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n// Minimal interface for CLPool (Solidity 0.7.6 compatible)\ninterface ICLPoolMinimal {\n    function syncReward(uint256 _rewardRate, uint256 _rewardReserve, uint256 _periodFinish) external;\n    function updateRewardsGrowthGlobal() external;\n    function stake(int128 stakedLiquidityDelta, int24 tickLower, int24 tickUpper, bool positionUpdate) external;\n    function rewardReserve() external view returns (uint256);\n    function rollover() external view returns (uint256);\n    function stakedLiquidity() external view returns (uint128);\n    function rewardGrowthGlobalX128() external view returns (uint256);\n    function gauge() external view returns (address);\n    function rewardRate() external view returns (uint256);\n    function lastUpdated() external view returns (uint32);\n}\ninterface ICLPoolFactory {\n        function createPool(address tokenA, address tokenB, int24 tickSpacing, uint160 sqrtPriceX96)\n        external\n        returns (address pool);\n}\n\n// Simple Mock ERC20 for compatibility\ncontract MockERC20 {\n    string public name;\n    string public symbol;\n    uint8 public decimals;\n    \n    mapping(address => uint256) public balanceOf;\n    mapping(address => mapping(address => uint256)) public allowance;\n    \n    function initialize(string memory _name, string memory _symbol, uint8 _decimals) external {\n        name = _name;\n        symbol = _symbol;\n        decimals = _decimals;\n    }\n    \n    function approve(address spender, uint256 amount) external returns (bool) {\n        allowance[msg.sender][spender] = amount;\n        return true;\n    }\n    \n    function transfer(address to, uint256 amount) external returns (bool) {\n        balanceOf[msg.sender] -= amount;\n        balanceOf[to] += amount;\n        return true;\n    }\n    \n    function transferFrom(address from, address to, uint256 amount) external returns (bool) {\n        if (allowance[from][msg.sender] != type(uint256).max) {\n            allowance[from][msg.sender] -= amount;\n        }\n        balanceOf[from] -= amount;\n        balanceOf[to] += amount;\n        return true;\n    }\n}\n```",
